{
  "name": "overwall_vent_sky_falloff",
  "description": "Follow-up to the vent report: the player narrowed it to Replace Stuff's OVER-WALL vent (Vent_Over) and blamed the way that mod puts a building into a wall's own cell, which is exactly right. Vent_Over is an edifice in its 1.6 def (the isEdifice=false its pre-1.6 def carried is gone), and EdificeGrid.Register just writes the cell's one slot -- so building a vent onto a wall EVICTS that wall from the edifice grid while the wall goes on standing there, and a blocker test that asks the edifice grid sees a blockLight=false vent where a granite wall is. Five 11x11 roofed rooms along z=105, identical but for the middle cell of the south wall: (-39) unbroken granite control, (-13) a wall with a Vent_Over built onto it in that order via StackThing -- the reported case -- (13) a Vent_Over with no wall under it, which Replace Stuff's PlaceWorker_Vent prefix makes buildable and whose def has blockLight FALSE, (39) a core Vent alone, re-measuring the fix already shipped in the same frame, and (65) the same pair as (-13) in the opposite order, which is not player-reachable and is kept because it reads CLEAN on the broken build: PlaceThings cannot spawn onto a wall cell, so the first version of this scenario built that arrangement and reported no bug at all. Every arm's *_depth must read 0. The CellBlockerProbe pins at the gap cell say why, separating what our flood used to ask (edifice_blocks) from what vanilla's glow grid holds (any_blocks), proving the wall was not wiped (buildings=2) and ruling out a lost roof. The first capture is discarded (overwall_vent_hud_discard.png) because hideUi is only honoured from the second onward, and the frame the A/B is measured on must not carry the HUD's run-to-run message log. Forces the Realistic preset and runs without Ambient Light for the same reasons native_sky_falloff.json gives.",
  "saveFile": "minimal_colony.rws",
